1
00:01:27,440 --> 00:01:33,000
In the previous episode of Flash & Dash, the racing legend Elvin was unable to attend the racing championship.

2
00:01:33,160 --> 00:01:38,260
Isaac, who had been playing with Elvin's tactics, caught the attention of national champion Carson.

3
00:01:38,620 --> 00:01:42,700
In their race, Carson's Storm Blade destroyed Isaac's car.

4
00:01:42,900 --> 00:01:47,480
Carson felt bad and found a new car at the club called Flash Mirage.

5
00:01:48,060 --> 00:01:49,400
Episode 2: FLASH MIRAGE

5.1
00:02:09,760 --> 00:02:11,700
Come on! Show me your skills.

5.2
00:02:17,160 --> 00:02:18,500
What happened?

5.3
00:02:18,860 --> 00:02:21,500
I used the usual method to take the curve.

5.4
00:02:24,160 --> 00:02:26,500
No way! I can't slow down.

5.5
00:02:30,160 --> 00:02:34,500
Impossible! I'm in the lowest gear, why can't I control it?

6
00:02:48,460 --> 00:02:53,140
He got too close to the roadside, but the car is still shaking.

7
00:02:53,780 --> 00:02:54,500
This car...

7
00:03:01,780 --> 00:03:03,000
You! What are you doing here?

8
00:03:03,500 --> 00:03:07,060
This car has the latest remote control technology.

9
00:03:07,060 --> 00:03:10,500
Its parts are also the lightest parts in the world.

10
00:03:11,180 --> 00:03:15,460
It is manufactured to be very light in order to make a quick takeoff.

11
00:03:16,460 --> 00:03:18,780
What? How do you know all this?

12
00:03:19,120 --> 00:03:22,940
Our Mina is the best remote control technician in our unit.

13
00:03:23,240 --> 00:03:26,240
She can understand the configuration of cars at a glance.

14
00:03:26,420 --> 00:03:28,840
Whatever car it is, she figures it out immediately.

15
00:03:29,180 --> 00:03:30,960
So why did you come here?

16
00:03:31,720 --> 00:03:33,980
You're the one who destroyed Isaac's car.

17
00:03:34,280 --> 00:03:36,400
You'll take responsibility for it, right?

18
00:03:36,400 --> 00:03:38,780
I see you have a lot of cars in your club.

19
00:03:39,220 --> 00:03:40,700
I think this car is suitable for us.

20
00:03:40,920 --> 00:03:43,080
Consider that I bought it from you.

21
00:03:43,260 --> 00:03:43,420
Huh?

22
00:03:44,400 --> 00:03:46,620
I would never give that car away.

23
00:03:47,600 --> 00:03:48,280
You...

24
00:03:48,840 --> 00:03:50,340
Forget it Mina, it's okay.

25
00:03:50,760 --> 00:03:52,580
But you don't have a car right now.

26
00:03:52,800 --> 00:03:53,840
And besides...

27
00:03:53,840 --> 00:03:56,820
For a racer, his car is of great importance.

28
00:03:57,160 --> 00:03:58,980
As a racer...

29
00:03:58,980 --> 00:04:01,640
...I can't take someone's car like this.

30
00:04:02,580 --> 00:04:03,620
Here's the car.

31
00:04:03,940 --> 00:04:04,280
Here you go.

32
00:04:09,850 --> 00:04:11,130
Come on Mina.

33
00:04:11,490 --> 00:04:12,290
Let's get out of here.

34
00:04:13,630 --> 00:04:14,090
Isaac.

34.1
00:04:21,630 --> 00:04:22,090
Push it!

35
00:04:31,040 --> 00:04:32,320
Isaac, buddy.

36
00:04:32,520 --> 00:04:33,480
You came just in time.

37
00:04:33,820 --> 00:04:36,200
Hey man, teach us how to race.

38
00:04:36,620 --> 00:04:37,280
Yeah, yeah.

39
00:04:37,720 --> 00:04:39,860
Show us how you do the Speed Stream.

40
00:04:40,680 --> 00:04:41,080
Well...

41
00:04:42,360 --> 00:04:44,460
Do it so we can watch you.

42
00:04:45,900 --> 00:04:46,460
Huh?

43
00:04:47,420 --> 00:04:48,820
What do you want?

44
00:04:49,220 --> 00:04:51,980
We heard you're the best racer around here.

45
00:04:52,100 --> 00:04:53,860
So we came to race against you.

46
00:04:54,060 --> 00:04:55,680
I can't deal with you right now.

47
00:04:57,970 --> 00:04:59,690
Aren't you a racing master?

48
00:05:00,070 --> 00:05:01,350
Where's your car then?

49
00:05:01,910 --> 00:05:02,370
Ah.

50
00:05:02,510 --> 00:05:03,530
I almost forgot.

51
00:05:03,790 --> 00:05:06,390
Your car was wrecked by the national champion.

52
00:05:07,890 --> 00:05:10,330
You can't race us even if you wanted to.

53
00:05:11,070 --> 00:05:12,610
Get out of here right now.

54
00:05:13,490 --> 00:05:17,030
Isaac doesn't need to bother defeating you.

55
00:05:17,150 --> 00:05:18,070
I can beat you myself.

56
00:05:31,990 --> 00:05:33,110
Sonic Blast.

57
00:05:33,310 --> 00:05:35,830
You're going to beat us with such a bulky car, huh?

58
00:05:35,830 --> 00:05:38,890
When the race is over, we'll see who's winning.

59
00:05:43,230 --> 00:05:44,770
Three-Two-One-Go!

60
00:05:57,740 --> 00:05:58,400
No way.

61
00:05:58,580 --> 00:06:00,380
Now I'll show you my real power.

62
00:06:07,420 --> 00:06:08,340
Come on.

62.1
00:06:09,420 --> 00:06:11,040
This isn't fair!

62.2
00:06:15,420 --> 00:06:16,040
What!

62.2
00:06:17,120 --> 00:06:19,040
You're going to pass me? No way!

63
00:06:22,120 --> 00:06:24,320
My Sonic Blast may not be as fast as yours.

64
00:06:24,480 --> 00:06:25,360
But it's powerful.

65
00:06:25,820 --> 00:06:27,640
No car can be this strong.

66
00:06:27,940 --> 00:06:30,320
It's not that easy to pass my car.

67
00:06:43,100 --> 00:06:43,860
No way.

68
00:06:56,370 --> 00:06:57,830
You think you're going to win?

68
00:07:03,370 --> 00:07:06,830
Free Speed Turn!!

69
00:06:27,830 --> 00:07:29,220
How is this possible?

70
00:07:29,700 --> 00:07:32,960
Now you know what my Sonic Blast can do.

71
00:07:33,140 --> 00:07:35,040
You won't bother anyone after this.

72
00:07:38,020 --> 00:07:38,280
Hah.

73
00:07:38,780 --> 00:07:39,800
Wait for me.

74
00:07:40,320 --> 00:07:40,980
Stop.

75
00:07:41,180 --> 00:07:42,820
You still have to apologize to Isaac.

76
00:07:43,520 --> 00:07:43,660
Aha.

77
00:07:44,640 --> 00:07:45,760
Let it go, Mina.

78
00:07:45,920 --> 00:07:46,540
Let them go.

79
00:07:46,760 --> 00:07:49,800
When you meet these types, you'll teach them a lesson.

80
00:07:50,540 --> 00:07:51,240
Mina.

81
00:07:51,400 --> 00:07:53,200
Were you able to repair my car?

82
00:07:54,020 --> 00:07:55,700
I did my best.

83
00:07:55,940 --> 00:07:57,000
I think it might work.

84
00:07:57,420 --> 00:07:59,180
Its functionality isn't like before.

85
00:08:01,120 --> 00:08:02,000
Here.

86
00:08:02,280 --> 00:08:04,020
I'm afraid it can't enter any race.

87
00:08:04,640 --> 00:08:05,340
Huh.

88
00:08:09,580 --> 00:08:10,600
What about this?

89
00:08:10,760 --> 00:08:12,780
I can give you Sonic Blast.

90
00:08:13,620 --> 00:08:15,820
Sonic Blast is your everything.

91
00:08:15,940 --> 00:08:16,820
I can't accept it.

92
00:08:16,960 --> 00:08:18,180
It's too late.

93
00:08:18,880 --> 00:08:19,980
I'll go home.

94
00:08:46,980 --> 00:08:47,540
Isaac.

95
00:08:47,820 --> 00:08:48,700
My child.

96
00:08:50,340 --> 00:08:52,060
Grandma, let me help you.

97
00:08:52,700 --> 00:08:54,960
Why didn't you go to the race today?

98
00:08:55,840 --> 00:08:59,400
Well, I'm a bit tired, so I came home early.

99
00:08:59,760 --> 00:09:02,620
Or is there some problem with your car?

100
00:09:02,860 --> 00:09:03,940
What problem, dear?

101
00:09:04,440 --> 00:09:07,020
Remember, I'm a master at racing.

102
00:09:07,220 --> 00:09:08,640
No one can touch my car.

103
00:09:09,220 --> 00:09:10,380
Okay, grandma?

104
00:09:10,920 --> 00:09:11,720
Don't worry.

105
00:09:12,080 --> 00:09:13,520
Shall I help you cook?

106
00:09:13,520 --> 00:09:14,500
Hmm.

107
00:09:24,320 --> 00:09:25,160
Dad.

108
00:09:25,620 --> 00:09:26,560
Tell me, Carson.

109
00:09:28,880 --> 00:09:31,140
I'm going to ask something about this car.

110
00:09:31,520 --> 00:09:33,180
Or is this car...

111
00:09:34,140 --> 00:09:35,820
Dad, I'm sorry.

112
00:09:35,980 --> 00:09:37,840
I took this car without permission.

113
00:09:38,100 --> 00:09:40,160
You must have tried it out.

114
00:09:40,480 --> 00:09:41,340
What do you think?

115
00:09:41,340 --> 00:09:44,680
Controlling Flash Mirage was harder than I thought.

116
00:09:44,980 --> 00:09:47,340
I wanted to control it the normal way.

117
00:09:47,820 --> 00:09:51,040
Before I even increased the power, it almost went off the road.

118
00:09:51,480 --> 00:09:52,920
I couldn't control it.

119
00:09:53,980 --> 00:09:54,760
Dad.

120
00:09:54,940 --> 00:09:56,140
Can you tell me what the problem is?

121
00:09:57,080 --> 00:10:00,500
To tell you the truth, I made this car for Elvin.

122
00:10:00,880 --> 00:10:01,620
I don't understand.

123
00:10:01,700 --> 00:10:01,920
What did you say?

124
00:10:01,960 --> 00:10:06,100
Do you know why everyone admires a talented racer like Elvin?

125
00:10:08,930 --> 00:10:11,490
It's solely because of his rebellious racing style.

126
00:10:11,490 --> 00:10:18,830
No matter how sharp the curve, he wouldn't slow down, and no one else could attempt this very dangerous and challenging path.

127
00:10:19,070 --> 00:10:24,890
Although he hasn't participated in the racing championship in recent years, I often come across his racing statistics.

128
00:10:25,090 --> 00:10:28,470
This car was designed according to his racing style.

129
00:10:33,040 --> 00:10:38,380
And he discovered this style when he used the Speed Stream.

130
00:10:46,100 --> 00:10:46,900
Too bad.

131
00:10:47,140 --> 00:10:50,800
In the past years, I didn't get the chance to race against him.

132
00:10:50,800 --> 00:10:58,260
If you can't control the car either, unfortunately, no other racer can.

133
00:10:59,220 --> 00:11:00,960
Maybe someone can, dad.

134
00:11:01,680 --> 00:11:04,160
Could you give Flash Mirage to me, perhaps?

135
00:11:04,980 --> 00:11:07,500
But you already have Storm Blade, son.

136
00:11:07,880 --> 00:11:09,000
I'll give it to someone.

137
00:11:09,360 --> 00:11:12,040
Maybe he can control a car that I can't.

138
00:11:45,740 --> 00:11:47,900
Come on, let's practice.

139
00:11:55,700 --> 00:11:58,660
How is this possible? I can't control my car.

139.1
00:12:10,700 --> 00:12:12,760
No way! Stop already.

139.2
00:12:22,700 --> 00:12:24,960
No...!

140
00:12:32,360 --> 00:12:33,180
You!

140.1
00:12:35,360 --> 00:12:36,780
What are you doing here?

141
00:12:37,100 --> 00:12:39,000
And with such a bulky car.

142
00:12:39,540 --> 00:12:40,440
Is it worth it?

143
00:12:40,440 --> 00:12:42,420
You don't understand me at all.

144
00:12:43,920 --> 00:12:47,000
That was the first gift my grandmother gave me.

145
00:12:47,220 --> 00:12:48,440
It was also my only friend.

146
00:12:48,580 --> 00:12:51,900
Even so, is it worth risking your life, tell me.

147
00:12:53,040 --> 00:12:56,240
If you get hurt, we'll all be sad for you.

148
00:12:57,260 --> 00:12:59,020
If you want it so badly.

149
00:13:00,920 --> 00:13:02,620
We can race again.

150
00:13:03,040 --> 00:13:05,700
If you win, you can take Flash Mirage from me.

151
00:13:05,700 --> 00:13:09,260
This time I'll beat you without making any foul moves.

152
00:13:09,540 --> 00:13:11,480
Save those words for yourself.

153
00:13:14,100 --> 00:13:16,870
Of course you'll race him since he's back on his feet.

154
00:13:17,460 --> 00:13:19,400
And he'll show you his real power.

155
00:13:19,560 --> 00:13:22,020
This time you'll beat him and win the car.

156
00:13:30,010 --> 00:13:31,830
I don't accept your challenge.

157
00:13:33,450 --> 00:13:34,560
Why not?

158
00:13:35,070 --> 00:13:36,570
This is an unmissable opportunity.

159
00:13:36,730 --> 00:13:38,550
With this, you could have a brand new car.

160
00:13:40,390 --> 00:13:43,170
Don't tell me you're afraid of losing.

161
00:13:43,330 --> 00:13:46,330
A rich person like you has lots of cars at home.

162
00:13:46,550 --> 00:13:49,230
You never value the car you have.

163
00:13:49,750 --> 00:13:51,850
Cars cannot be made into playthings.

164
00:13:52,090 --> 00:13:56,810
People like you will never understand the importance of a racing car to its owner.

165
00:14:08,090 --> 00:14:10,070
It's just a bulky car.

166
00:14:10,250 --> 00:14:11,330
What's there to be so proud of?

167
00:14:28,230 --> 00:14:29,610
I'm sorry, ma'am.

168
00:14:29,790 --> 00:14:30,290
Are you okay?

169
00:14:30,410 --> 00:14:31,150
It was an accident.

170
00:14:32,170 --> 00:14:33,170
I'm fine.

171
00:14:33,430 --> 00:14:33,770
I'm fine.

172
00:14:36,840 --> 00:14:38,220
I'm sorry, sir.

173
00:14:38,860 --> 00:14:39,520
Thanks.

174
00:14:40,080 --> 00:14:40,240
Oh.

175
00:14:40,700 --> 00:14:43,000
Are you a remote control car racer?

176
00:14:43,240 --> 00:14:43,740
Yes.

177
00:14:43,740 --> 00:14:45,700
Or are you interested in them?

178
00:14:45,900 --> 00:14:46,120
No.

179
00:14:46,540 --> 00:14:49,640
I want to buy a new car for my grandson.

180
00:14:49,940 --> 00:14:50,120
Ah.

181
00:14:50,740 --> 00:14:52,660
Don't look down on him.

182
00:14:52,880 --> 00:14:53,720
He's young.

183
00:14:53,920 --> 00:14:59,720
But my handsome grandson is one of the best car racers in this area.

184
00:15:00,080 --> 00:15:00,380
Hm.

185
00:15:13,320 --> 00:15:15,360
His car broke down the other day.

186
00:15:15,600 --> 00:15:17,760
He can't participate in car races anymore.

187
00:15:17,980 --> 00:15:21,120
So I want to buy him a brand new car.

188
00:15:22,480 --> 00:15:25,580
Could your grandson's name be Isaac, perhaps?

189
00:15:26,180 --> 00:15:27,640
How do you know?

190
00:15:28,120 --> 00:15:28,300
Ah.

191
00:15:29,260 --> 00:15:29,900
Well, I...

192
00:15:30,160 --> 00:15:32,200
Actually, I was the one who wrecked his car.

193
00:15:32,540 --> 00:15:32,840
Oh.

194
00:15:36,140 --> 00:15:36,460
Ah.

195
00:15:36,560 --> 00:15:37,040
That's it.

196
00:15:37,160 --> 00:15:38,920
It never crossed my mind.

197
00:15:39,460 --> 00:15:40,540
I'm sorry, ma'am.

198
00:15:40,840 --> 00:15:43,260
If I hadn't wrecked it, his car would have been just fine.

199
00:15:43,540 --> 00:15:44,960
And you wouldn't be so upset.

200
00:15:46,000 --> 00:15:47,720
Please don't say that.

201
00:15:48,140 --> 00:15:49,700
It's me who should apologize.

202
00:15:49,780 --> 00:15:49,920
Ah.

203
00:15:51,380 --> 00:15:53,500
Isaac's parents worked away from home.

204
00:15:56,500 --> 00:15:59,020
Since he was a baby, he's been staying with me.

205
00:16:03,100 --> 00:16:05,890
He has always been a very well-behaved child.

206
00:16:06,450 --> 00:16:07,810
He helped me.

207
00:16:09,380 --> 00:16:15,270
So he never really had the opportunity to make other friends in his life.

208
00:16:16,050 --> 00:16:19,850
Likewise, he had very few friends to play with.

209
00:16:22,850 --> 00:16:25,530
I bought him a remote control racing car.

210
00:16:25,890 --> 00:16:28,110
He got so attached to that car.

211
00:16:28,650 --> 00:16:31,570
The car became his one and only true friend.

212
00:16:49,820 --> 00:16:52,420
That's why he's angry at you.

213
00:16:52,640 --> 00:16:53,900
Please don't be mad at him.

214
00:16:54,900 --> 00:16:56,860
You want to help him.

215
00:16:57,080 --> 00:16:59,160
On his behalf, I apologize to you very much.

216
00:16:59,460 --> 00:17:00,320
Don't say that.

217
00:17:01,000 --> 00:17:02,620
I caused all of this.

218
00:17:03,100 --> 00:17:03,980
I'm responsible.

219
00:17:04,340 --> 00:17:07,760
And I really don't want Isaac to lose the race because of the car.

220
00:17:07,760 --> 00:17:12,760
But knowing Isaac's character, I don't think he'll accept this gesture.

221
00:17:13,760 --> 00:17:15,740
I can handle it.

222
00:17:16,220 --> 00:17:18,480
But I'll need your help.

223
00:17:25,080 --> 00:17:25,860
Isaac!

224
00:17:26,040 --> 00:17:26,840
Isaac!

225
00:17:27,400 --> 00:17:28,180
Is there a problem?

226
00:17:28,580 --> 00:17:30,900
I just met a kid.

227
00:17:31,420 --> 00:17:33,980
He spilled all the fruit from my stall and left.

228
00:17:34,200 --> 00:17:36,020
He didn't even apologize.

229
00:17:36,480 --> 00:17:38,780
He told me to tell Isaac to come find me.

230
00:17:39,320 --> 00:17:40,220
What are you saying?

231
00:17:40,440 --> 00:17:41,080
Where is this kid?

232
00:17:41,080 --> 00:17:44,460
He's waiting on the main street of our neighborhood.

233
00:17:48,400 --> 00:17:49,720
I knew it was you.

234
00:17:49,840 --> 00:17:50,740
What do you want from me?

235
00:17:54,080 --> 00:17:54,900
What happened?

236
00:17:55,260 --> 00:17:57,040
Are you going to avenge your grandmother?

237
00:17:57,420 --> 00:18:01,960
Since you saw my grandmother, you must be the one who set up the race.

238
00:18:02,700 --> 00:18:04,900
I'm not going to race you or anything.

239
00:18:05,140 --> 00:18:07,860
A real racer never backs down from any challenge.

240
00:18:08,080 --> 00:18:11,300
If you're a coward, how can you be a real racer?

241
00:18:15,140 --> 00:18:18,460
I hope you become an excellent racer in the future.

242
00:18:22,540 --> 00:18:23,080
Alright.

243
00:18:23,280 --> 00:18:24,600
I'll race you.

244
00:18:26,940 --> 00:18:29,160
We'll finish the race after five laps.

245
00:18:37,370 --> 00:18:40,250
This time I'll beat you fair and square.

246
00:18:41,230 --> 00:18:42,610
Let's see then.

247
00:18:42,830 --> 00:18:43,470
Let's start.

248
00:18:55,460 --> 00:19:02,200
Given Flash Mirage's new winning feature or its road holding for this lap, it's a much better car than my old ones.

249
00:19:02,200 --> 00:19:05,040
But it's hard to control.

250
00:19:19,360 --> 00:19:23,120
It's surprising how quickly you picked up the secret of rough roads.

251
00:19:24,020 --> 00:19:27,200
No road is an obstacle for me a second time.

252
00:19:27,300 --> 00:19:28,160
Watch now.

252.1
00:19:37,000 --> 00:19:38,160
No way!

253
00:19:39,820 --> 00:19:43,740
Although this car is very fast, its control is so different from other cars.

254
00:19:48,660 --> 00:19:51,640
This car is too fast, I can't control it properly.

255
00:19:52,460 --> 00:19:54,260
What kind of car is this?

256
00:20:14,460 --> 00:20:17,260
Let's see if you have that skill or not.

257
00:20:17,460 --> 00:20:19,260
Controlling Elvin's car is difficult.

258
